{"content":[{"c":["ELNATHAN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Grandfather of King Jehoiachin. His daughter, Jehoiachin’s mother, was Nehushta (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.24.8","r":"2Kgs.24.8","rawR":"2Kgs.24.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.24.8","value":"2Kgs.24.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 24:8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2, 3, 4. Three Jewish leaders whom Ezra sent to Iddo at Casiphia to obtain Levites and temple servants for the caravan of Jews returning to Palestine from Babylonia (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.8.16","r":"Ezra.8.16","rawR":"Ezra.8.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.8.16","value":"Ezra.8.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 8:16"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Acbor’s son, who was ordered by King Jehoiakim to bring back Uriah from Egypt to be executed for prophesying against the king (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.26.22-23","r":"Jer.26.22-23","rawR":"Jer.26.22-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.26.22-23","value":"Jer.26.22-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 26:22-23"},"). Elnathan was present with other princes when Baruch read the Lord’s words of warning written at Jeremiah’s dictation on a scroll (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.12","r":"Jer.36.12","rawR":"Jer.36.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.12","value":"Jer.36.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"36:12"},"); he tried unsuccessfully to prevent Jehoiakim from burning the scroll (v ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.36.25","r":"Jer.36.25","rawR":"Jer.36.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.36.25","value":"Jer.36.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"25"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Elnathan","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 24:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.24.8","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.24.8","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.24.8"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 8:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.8.16","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.8.16","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.8.16"},{"anchorText":"Jer 26:22-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.26.22-23","rawQueryValue":"Jer.26.22-23","sourceRefExact":"Jer.26.22-23"},{"anchorText":"36:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.12","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.12","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.12"},{"anchorText":"25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.36.25","rawQueryValue":"Jer.36.25","sourceRefExact":"Jer.36.25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b0124b516a1f192afbb000a2bbe0926a59ca96deccfea7ef6eb956e640ada675","sourceItemName":"Elnathan","sourceItemOrder":130,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Elnathan","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Elnathan","title":"Elnathan","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}